// Import a spec written with Spec Kit or OpenSpec, or in a document: {{spec}}
// A Spec Kit feature (specs/NNN-name: spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md), an OpenSpec change
// (openspec/changes/<id>: proposal.md, tasks.md, spec deltas) or a Word or Markdown document
// on SharePoint or OneDrive (read through Work IQ) becomes the claims: one
// per user story, functional requirement and success criterion (or per added and
// modified requirement), each proven by the folder's tests or a sign-off. The spec is
// saved as knowledge the steps are given, so the peers need no copy of it.
// Vars: spec (the feature's folder, or the document's https:// link), peer, folder,
// reviewers (a squad), test, approver
claim: STORIES Every user story works as its acceptance scenarios say
claim: RULES Every functional requirement holds, each proven by a test named after it
claim: OUTCOMES The success criteria are met
impl @{{peer}}:{{folder}} skill=implement-change verify={{test}} attempts=3 claims=STORIES,RULES Implement the feature as its spec, plan and tasks say (the tasks in order, ticked off as they are done), with a test for every acceptance scenario and requirement named after its claim id.
verify after impl #{{reviewers}}:{{folder}} skill=code-review apply=impl verify={{test}} claims=STORIES,RULES Review the change against the spec: does every acceptance scenario and requirement have a test that really proves it? Report each gap.
signoff after verify approve @{{approver}} claims=OUTCOMES Accept the feature: its success criteria are met.
